riptions point at sase/memory/sase_sizes.md instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]restating it — so the generated size note is genuinely the single [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]source of size truth, and epic sase-il can then be closed out.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]finish_tale_size_semantics.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/finish_tale_size_semantics.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]202608/sase_sizes_memory.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-il.7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-il/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-il.7.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Complete the tale size contract in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-tale-size-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-tale-size-contract: restrict tale `size` to xsmall/small/medium, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the launch-mode normalization the design specified, reduce the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]size/model field descriptions to pointers at the canonical size memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]note, and cut a sase-core release.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the completed contract in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sase-adopt-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-tale-size-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-adopt-contract: raise the sase-core-rs floor to the new release, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete the Python launch-compatibility shim now that core owns it, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate the 21 