om/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-il/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Robust long-note parent support[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-parent[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-parent: make a long memory note parented by another long note a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]first-class, validated arrangement across `sase memory init`, `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory read`, and memory proposals.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generated sase_sizes.md memory note[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sizes-memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after memory-parent[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sizes-memory: add the generated `sase/memory/sase_sizes.md` long note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parented by `sase/memory/sase_beads.md` and make it the only place [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-size guidance lives.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required tale size in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-tale-size[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-tale-size: require and validate a tale plan's `size` frontmatter in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase-core plan validator, expose it on the wire, and release it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt tale size in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plan-size-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sizes-memory, core-tale-size[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan-size-adopt: raise the sase-core floor, plumb the validated tale [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`size` through the Python adapter, and point every remaining size [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction at the memory note.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the coder alias bucket[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]coder-alias[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plan-size-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]coder-alias: delete the `coder` and `<provider>_coder` implicit aliases [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and route coder follow-ups through the phase-worker alias for the tale [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan's size.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Verify plan handoff for large task beads[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]task-plan-handoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-plan-handoff: audit and regression-test that every task-bead launch[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path appends `#plan` for `large` and `xlarge` task beads.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-il","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-il.2","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a30e760c740fd22a21e56cbe10258a1a","started_at":"2026-08-10T11:22:55.966877+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786311823,"sha":"46fbdc07a158cb4f97ce2c70913dd146fb6b0cc8","subject":"feat!: require tale size in SASE plan validation"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"b90ca4124bf1b14d223de54bc369480bf5804f060982d687e2e82808d524f494","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-il.3/chat.md","size_bytes":38561},"commits":{"digest":"567fac21e90819df5509dd720597844959b464c31b48abda299873ec618ce632","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-il.3/commits.json","size_bytes":226},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d52966